{"questions":[{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d148607886","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d148607886","q":"<p>Suppose that X is waiting time in minutes for a bus and its p.d.f. is given by f(x) = `1/5`, for 0 ≤ x ≤ 5 and = 0 otherwise.</p>\n<p>Find the probability that waiting time is between 1 and 3.</p><br><br><p>Suppose that X is waiting time in minutes for a bus and its p.d.f. is given by f(x) = `1/5`, for 0 ≤ x ≤ 5 and = 0 otherwise.</p>\n<p>Find the probability that the waiting time is more than 4 minutes.</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Required probability P(1 &lt; X &lt; 3)</p>\n<p>= `int_(1)^3 f(x) dx`</p>\n<p>= `int_(1)^3 1/5 (x) dx`</p>\n<p>= `int_(1)^3 1/5  1 dx`</p>\n<p>= `1/5  [x]_1^3`</p>\n<p>= `1/5 [3 - 1]`</p>\n<p>= `2/5`</p><br><br><p>Required probability P(X &gt; 4)</p>\n<p>= `int_(4)^∞ f (x)dx`</p>\n<p>= `int_(4)^5 f (x)dx`+` int_(5)^∞ f (x)dx`</p>\n<p>= `int_(4)^5 1/5 dx + 0`</p>\n<p>= `1/5 int_(4)^5 1dx`</p>\n<p>= `1/5[x]_4^5`</p>\n<p>= `1/5 [5 - 4]`</p>\n<p>= `1/5`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Probability Distributions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2025","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2025","paperDate":"2025-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d14860785a","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d14860785a","q":"<p>Find the probability distribution of number of heads in two tosses of a coin.</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>When one coin is tossed twice, the sample space is</p>\n<p>{HH, HT, TH, TT}</p>\n<p>Let X represent the number of heads s in two tosses of a coin.</p>\n<p>∴ X(HH) = 2,</p>\n<p>X(HT) = 1,</p>\n<p>X(TH) = 1,</p>\n<p>X(TT) = 0</p>\n<p>Therefore, X can take the value of 0, 1 or 2.</p>\n<p>It is known that,</p>\n<p>P(HH) = P(HT) = P(TH) = P(TT) = `1/4`</p>\n<p>P(X = 0) = P(TT) = `1/4`</p>\n<p>P(X = 1) = P(HT) + P(TH) = `1/4 +1/4 = 1/2`</p>\n<p>P(X = 2) = P(HH) = `1/4`</p>\n<p>Thus, the required probability distribution is as follows:</p>\n<table border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>X</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>P(X)</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">`1/4`</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">`1/2`</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">`1/4`</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Probability Distributions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperDate":"2024-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d14860782d","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d14860782d","q":"<p>Find the mean of number randomly selected from 1 to 15.</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>The sample space of the experiment is S = {1, 2, 3, …, 15}.</p>\n<p>Let X denotes the number selected.</p>\n<p>Then X is a random variable that can take values 1, 2, 3, …, 15.</p>\n<p>Each number selected is equiprobable therefore</p>\n<p>P(1) = P(2) = P(3) = … = P(15) = `1/15`</p>\n<p>μ = E(X) = `sum_(i = 1)^n x_ip_i`</p>\n<p>= `1 xx 1/15 + 2 xx 1/15 + 3 xx 1/15 + ... + 15 xx 1/15`</p>\n<p>= `(1 + 2 + 3 + ... + 15) xx 1/15`</p>\n<p>= `((15 xx 16)/2) xx 1/15`</p>\n<p>= 8</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Probability Distributions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperDate":"2023-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077f2","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077f2","q":"<p>If the p.m.f of a r. v. X is</p>\n<p>P(x) = `c/x^3`, for x = 1, 2, 3</p>\n<p>        = 0, otherwise</p>\n<p>then E(X) = ______.</p>","options":["<p>`216/251`</p>","<p>`294/251`</p>","<p>`297/294`</p>","<p>`294/297`</p>"],"answer":1,"solution":"<p>If the p.m.f of a r. v. X is</p>\n<p>P(x) = `c/x^3`, for x = 1, 2, 3</p>\n<p>        = 0, otherwise</p>\n<p>then E(X) = `bb(294/251)`.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Probability Distributions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"singleCorrect","source":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperDate":"2022-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077b3","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077b3","q":"<p>Let the p. m. f. of a random variable X be __</p>\n<p>P(x) = `(3-x)/10` for x = -1,0,1,2</p>\n<p>= 0                        otherwise</p>\n<p>Then E(X ) is ________.</p>","options":["<p>1</p>","<p>2</p>","<p>0</p>","<p>-1</p>"],"answer":2,"solution":"<p><strong>0</strong></p>\n<table border=\"1\" style=\"width: 41.0145%; height: 55px;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px;\">x</td>\n<td style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px;\">-1</td>\n<td style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px;\">2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px;\">P(x)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px;\">`4/10`</td>\n<td style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px;\">`3/10`</td>\n<td style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px;\">`2/10`</td>\n<td style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px;\">`1/10`</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px;\">x.P(x)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px;\">`(-4)/10`</td>\n<td style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px;\">`2/10`</td>\n<td style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px;\">`2/10`</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>`sum x.P(x) = 0`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Probability Distributions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"singleCorrect","source":"HSC Boards - 2018","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2018","paperDate":"2018-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d148607865","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d148607865","q":"<p><strong>Find k, if the following function is p.d.f. of r.v.X:</strong></p>\n<p>f(x) = `{:(kx^2(1 - x)\",\", \"for\"  0 &lt; x &lt; 1),(0\",\", \"otherwise\"):}`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Since f(x) is p.d.f. of r.v.X, we get</p>\n<p>`int_-∞^∞ f(x) dx` = 1</p>\n<p>∴ `int_-∞^0 f(x)dx + int_0^1 f(x)dx + int_1^∞ f(x)dx` = 1 </p>\n<p>∴ `0 + int_0^1 kx^2 (1 - x)dx + 0` = 1</p>\n<p>∴ `kint_0^1 (x^2 - x^3)dx` = 1</p>\n<p>∴ `k[x^3/3 - x^4/4]_0^1` = 1</p>\n<p>∴ `k[(1/3 - 1/4) - 0]` = 1</p>\n<p>∴ `k(1/12)` = 1</p>\n<p>∴ k = 12</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Probability Distributions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperDate":"2024-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d148607839","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d148607839","q":"<p>For the following probability density function of a random variable X, find P(X &lt; 1).</p>\n<p>`{:(f(x) = (x + 2)/18,\";\"  \"for\" -2 &lt; x &lt; 4),(               = 0,\",\"  \"otherwise\"):}`</p><br><br><p>For the following probability density function of a random variable X, find P(|X| &lt; 1).</p>\n<p>`{:(f(x) = (x + 2)/18,\";\"  \"for\" -2 &lt; x &lt; 4),(               = 0,\",\"  \"otherwise\"):}`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>P(X &lt; 1) = `int_-2^1 (x + 2)/18 dx`</p>\n<p>= `1/18 [x^2/2 + 2x]_-2^1`</p>\n<p>= `1/18 {(1/2 + 2) - ((-2)^2/2 + 2(-2))}`</p>\n<p>= `1/18 {5/2 + 2}`</p>\n<p>= `1/18 xx 9/2`</p>\n<p>= `1/4`</p>\n<p>P(X &lt; 1) = `1/4`</p><br><br><p>P(|X| &lt; 1) = P(–1 &lt; x &lt; 1)</p>\n<p>= `int_-1^1 (x + 2)/18 dx`</p>\n<p>= `1/18 [x^2/2 + 2x]_-1^1`</p>\n<p>= `1/18 {(1/2 + 2) - (1/2 - 2)}`</p>\n<p>= `1/18 {5/2 + 3/2}`</p>\n<p>= `1/18 xx 4`</p>\n<p>= `2/9`</p>\n<p>P(|X| &lt; 1) = `2/9`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Probability Distributions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperDate":"2023-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d14860780d","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d14860780d","q":"<p>Two dice are thrown simultaneously. If X denotes the number of sixes, find the expectation of X.</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Here, X represents the number of sixes obtained when two dice are thrown simultaneously. Therefore, X can take the value of 0, 1, or 2.</p>\n<p>∴ P (X = 0) = P (not getting six on any of the dice)</p>\n<p>= `(5 xx 5)/(6 xx 6)`</p>\n<p>= `25/36`</p>\n<p>P (X = 1) = P (six on first die and no six on second die) + P (no six on first die and six on second die)</p>\n<p>= `2(1/6xx5/6)`</p>\n<p>= `10/36`</p>\n<p>P (X = 2) = P (six on both the dice) =`1/36`</p>\n<p>∴ The required probability distribution is as follows.</p>\n<table border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>X</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>P(X)</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">`25/36`</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">`10/36`</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">`1/36`</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Expectation of X = E(X) = `sum X_iP(X_i)`</p>\n<p>= `0 xx 25/36 + 1 xx10/36 + 2xx 1/36`</p>\n<p>= `1/3`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Probability Distributions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperDate":"2022-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077db","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077db","q":"<table border=\"1\" style=\"width: 100%; height: 50px;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 25px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 16.6667%; height: 25px;\">x</td>\n<td style=\"width: 16.6667%; height: 25px;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"width: 16.6667%; height: 25px;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"width: 16.6667%; height: 25px;\">2</td>\n<td style=\"width: 16.6667%; height: 25px;\">3</td>\n<td style=\"width: 16.6667%; height: 25px;\">4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 25px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 16.6667%; height: 25px;\">P(X = x)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 16.6667%; height: 25px;\">0.45</td>\n<td style=\"width: 16.6667%; height: 25px;\">0.35</td>\n<td style=\"width: 16.6667%; height: 25px;\">0.15</td>\n<td style=\"width: 16.6667%; height: 25px;\">0.03</td>\n<td style=\"width: 16.6667%; height: 25px;\">0.02</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Find the variance of X.                                  </p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<table border=\"1\" style=\"width: 96.3731%; height: 178px;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 28px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 28px; text-align: center;\"><strong>x<sub>i</sub></strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 28px; text-align: center;\"><strong>p<sub>i</sub></strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 28px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.5px;\"><strong>p<sub>i</sub>x<sub>i</sub></strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 25.2674%; height: 28px; text-align: center;\"><strong>p<sub>i</sub>x<sub>i</sub><sup>2</sup></strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 25px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\">0.45</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25.2674%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 25px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\">0.35</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\">0.35</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25.2674%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\">0.35</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 25px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\">2</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\">0.15</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\">0.30</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25.2674%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\">0.60</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 25px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\">3</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\">0.03</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\">0.09</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25.2674%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\">0.27</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 25px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\">4</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\">0.02</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\">0.08</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25.2674%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\">0.32</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 25px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\"> </td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\">Total</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\">0.82</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25.2674%; height: 25px; text-align: center;\">1.54</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>E(X) = μ = ∑ p<sub>i</sub>x<sub>i</sub> = 0.82</p>\n<p>To find Var (X) use the formula : </p>\n<p>`\"Var\"(\"X\") = sum \"p\"_\"i\"\"x\"_\"i\"^2 - µ^2`</p>\n<p>= `1.54 - (0.82)^2`</p>\n<p>= 1.54 -0.6724</p>\n<p>= 0.8676</p>\n<p>Thus , Var (X) = 0.8676                               </p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Probability Distributions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2019","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2019","paperDate":"2019-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077dc","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077dc","q":"<p>For the following probability density function (p. d. f) of X, find P(X &lt; 1) and P(|x| &lt; 1) </p>\n<p>`f(x) = x^2/18, -3 &lt; x &lt; 3`</p>\n<p>            = 0,             otherwise</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>We have</p>\n<p>P(X &lt; 1) = `int_-3^1 f(x) dx`</p>\n<p>= `int_-3^1 x^2/18dx`</p>\n<p>= `[x^3/54]_-3^1`</p>\n<p>= `1/54 - ((-27)/54)`</p>\n<p>= `28/54`</p>\n<p>= `14/27`</p>\n<p>= 0.5185</p>\n<p>Now |X| &lt; 1</p>\n<p>`\\implies` ± X &lt; 1</p>\n<p>∴ X &lt; 1, – X &lt; 1,</p>\n<p>i.e. X &gt; – 1</p>\n<p>i.e. – 1 &lt; X &lt; 1</p>\n<p>∴ Required Probability = `int_-1^1 f(x)dx`</p>\n<p>= `int_-1^1 x^2/18dx`</p>\n<p>= `[x^3/54]_-1^1`</p>\n<p>= `1/54 + 1/54`</p>\n<p>= `2/54`</p>\n<p>= `1/27`</p>\n<p>= 0.03704</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Probability Distributions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2019","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2019","paperDate":"2019-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077c6","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077c6","q":"<p>Find the variance and standard deviation of the random variable X whose probability distribution is given below :</p>\n<table border=\"1\" style=\"width: 85.3832%; height: 44px;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 20.5202%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">x</td>\n<td style=\"width: 18.2081%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"width: 18.2081%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"width: 18.5694%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">2</td>\n<td style=\"width: 16.6907%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 20.5202%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">P(X = x)</td>\n<td style=\"width: 18.2081%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">`1/8`</td>\n<td style=\"width: 18.2081%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">`3/8`</td>\n<td style=\"width: 18.5694%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\">`3/8`</td>\n<td style=\"width: 16.6907%; text-align: center; height: 18px;\">`1/8`</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<table border=\"1\" style=\"width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 25%;\">`x_i`</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%;\">`p_i`</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%;\">`p_ix_i`</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%;\">`p_ix_i^2`</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 25%;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%;\">1/8</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%;\">0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 25%;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%;\">3/8</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%;\">3/8</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%;\">3/8</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 25%;\">2</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%;\">3/8</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%;\">6/8</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%;\">12/8</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 25%;\">3</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%;\">1/8</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%;\">3/8</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%;\">9/8</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 25%;\"> </td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%;\">Total</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%;\">12/8</td>\n<td style=\"width: 25%;\">24/8 = 3</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>`E(X) = mu = sump_ix_i = 12/8 = 3/2`</p>\n<p>`Var(X) = sum_(i=1)^n p_ix_i^2 - mu^2`</p>\n<p>`= 3 - (3/2)^2`</p>\n<p>`=3 - 9/4`</p>\n<p>`= 3/4`</p>\n<p>`∴ Var(X) = sigma^2 = 3/4`</p>\n<p>Standard deivation of (X) = `sigma_x = sqrt(3/4) =sqrt3/2`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Probability Distributions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2018","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2018","paperDate":"2018-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d14860779e","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d14860779e","q":"<p>Given the p. d. f. (probability density function) of a continuous random variable x as :</p>\n<p> `f(x)=x^2/3, -1`</p>\n<p>         = 0 , otherwise</p>\n<p>Determine the c. d. f. (cumulative distribution function) of x and hence find P(x &lt; 1), P(x ≤ -2), P(x &gt; 0), P(1 &lt; x &lt; 2)</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>c.d.f. of the continous random variable is given by</p>\n<p>`F(x)=int_-1^xy^2/3dx`</p>\n<p>`=[y^3/9]_-1^x`</p>\n<p>`=(x^3+1)/9, x in R`</p>\n<p>Consider P(X&lt;1)=F(1)=(1<sup>3</sup>+1)/9=2/9</p>\n<p>`P(x&lt;=-2)=0`</p>\n<p>`P(X&gt;0)=1-P(X&lt;=0)`</p>\n<p>`=1-F(0)`</p>\n<p>`=1-(0/9+1/9)`</p>\n<p>`=8/9`</p>\n<p>`P(1&lt;x&lt;2)=F(2) - F(1)`</p>\n<p>`=1-(1/9+1/9)`</p>\n<p>=`7/9`</p>\n<p> </p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Probability Distributions","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2017","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2017","paperDate":"2017-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"}]}